Now the Service. This is the biggest change. Modifications to PlayoutService.java:

1. `createAsset`: pass sponsorKey, return in response.
2. `publish`: add channel lock, window validation, sponsor snapshot, window hits. Refactor to share with batch publish.
3. New `batchPublish`.
4. New `revokePublication`, `getPublication`.
5. New window methods: `createSponsorWindow`, `reviseSponsorWindow`, `deleteSponsorWindow`, `getSponsorWindow`, `listSponsorWindows`.
6. `doCreateOverride`: add window check.
7. Helper: `validateSponsorExclusivity(channelId, segments with sponsor)` returning conflicts; throw 409 with details.

Design details:

For publish validation, I need segments with asset sponsor keys. In publish flow: after loading draft segments and grants, for each segment load asset (need sponsorKey). Assets were validated at draft time; they still exist (assets can't be deleted). Load asset sponsorKey via repo.findAsset.

Window validation per channel:
```java
private List<SponsorConflictDetail> validateSponsorWindows(String channelId, List<SegmentWithSponsor> segments) {
    List<SponsorConflictDetail> conflicts = new ArrayList<>();
    for (segment : segments) {
        if (segment.sponsorKey == null) continue;
        for (SponsorWindowRow w : repo.findActiveWindowsAt(channelId, seg.startMs, seg.endMs)) {
            if (!w.sponsorKey().equals(segment.sponsorKey)) {
                conflicts.add(new SponsorConflictDetail(channelId, atMs(seg.startMs), atMs(seg.endMs), seg.assetId, seg.sponsorKey, w.windowKey(), w.sponsorKey()));
            }
        }
    }
    return conflicts;
}
```

Throw ApiException with details — ApiException needs a details field. Let me extend ApiException with optional `List<SponsorConflictDetail> details` and a factory `sponsorConflict(List<SponsorConflictDetail>)`. GlobalExceptionHandler passes details into ErrorResponse.

For publish: lock channel first (lockChannelForUpdate) to serialize with window registration and override creation. Then do existing checks + window validation. Then insert publication, segments (with sponsorKey), and window hits (dedup by window id+channel).

Window hits: for each segment, findActiveWindowsAt(channel, seg.start, seg.end) — collect distinct (window.id, channelId). Record all hit windows regardless of sponsor.

Batch publish:
```java
@Transactional
public BatchPublishResponse batchPublish(BatchPublishRequest request) {
    if (request.items().isEmpty()) throw badRequest("批量发布条目不能为空");
    // hash over items
    return idempotent(request.requestId(), OP_BATCH_PUBLISH, hash, BatchPublishResponse.class, () -> {
        // lock all channels sorted
        // validate everything first (draft versions, published versions, grants, windows)
        // then commit all
    });
}
```

Structure: prepare per-item data (channel, draft, segments, grants, sponsors, conflicts) — validation phase collecting exceptions; then insert phase. To avoid duplicating publish logic, I'll write a private method `validatePublish(channelId, businessDay, draftVersion, expectedPublishedVersion)` returning a `PreparedPublish` record (channelId, businessDay, draft, segments, grantIds, sponsorKeys, windowHits), and `commitPublish(PreparedPublish)` returning PublishResponse. Single publish = validate + commit for one item. Batch = validate all, then commit all.

Note single publish currently doesn't lock channel. I'll add lockChannelForUpdate(channelId) at start of validation (both single and batch lock sorted unique channels).

For batch: lock channels in sorted order to avoid deadlock. Single publish locks its one channel. Override creation locks its channel. Window registration locks all its channels sorted. Consistent ordering → no deadlock.

Duplicate channel+day in batch items → 400/422? Two items for same channel+day would conflict on published version. I'll reject duplicates with 400 BAD_REQUEST ("批量发布包含重复的频道+业务日").

Revoke publication:
```java
@Transactional
public PublicationDetailResponse revokePublication(String channelId, long publicationId, String requestId) {
    String hash = sha256(OP_REVOKE_PUBLICATION + "|" + publicationId);
    return idempotent(requestId, OP_REVOKE_PUBLICATION, hash, PublicationDetailResponse.class, () -> {
        PublicationRow pub = repo.findPublicationForUpdate(publicationId)
            .orElseThrow(() -> notFound("发布快照不存在: " + publicationId));
        if (!pub.channelId().equals(channelId)) throw notFound(...);
        if (!pub.active()) throw conflict("PUBLICATION_ALREADY_REVOKED", ...);
        repo.lockChannelForUpdate(channelId);
        List<PublicationSegmentRow> segments = repo.findPublicationSegments(publicationId);
        long now = nowMs();
        boolean started = segments.stream().anyMatch(s -> s.startMs() <= now);
        if (started) throw conflict("PUBLICATION_ALREADY_STARTED", "发布已开始播出，只能按紧急插播流程处理: " + publicationId);
        repo.revokePublication(publicationId, requestId, now);
        return getPublication(channelId, publicationId);
    });
}
```

Wait — "尚未开始的发布" — publication hasn't started. Segments all in future: min(startMs) > now. If any segment.startMs <= now → started (even if all ended? If the whole day is past, it has "已经开始" — yes, started). Use anyMatch(startMs <= now). Empty segments → not started → revocable.

getPublication (read-only):
```java
@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public PublicationDetailResponse getPublication(String channelId, long publicationId) {
    PublicationRow pub = repo.findPublication(publicationId).orElseThrow(404);
    if (!pub.channelId().equals(channelId)) throw 404;
    segments → views; hits → views;
    return ...;
}
```

Window registration:
```java
@Transactional
public SponsorWindowResponse createSponsorWindow(CreateSponsorWindowRequest request) {
    String windowKey = blank ? UUID : request.windowKey();
    String hash = sha256(OP_CREATE_WINDOW + "|" + windowKey + "|" + sponsorKey + "|" + businessDay + "|" + canonicalChannels + "|" + startMs + "|" + endMs);
    return idempotent(request.requestId(), OP_CREATE_WINDOW, hash, SponsorWindowResponse.class, () -> {
        validateWindowParams(...); // 422 checks
        // channels exist → 404
        // lock channels sorted
        List<String> channels = sortedDistinct(request.channels());
        for (ch : channels) { repo.findChannel(ch).orElseThrow(404); }
        for (ch : channels) repo.lockChannelForUpdate(ch);
        if (repo.findLatestWindow(windowKey).isPresent()) throw conflict("DUPLICATE_WINDOW_KEY", ...);
        // overlap check per channel
        for (ch : channels) {
            List<SponsorWindowRow> overlaps = repo.findActiveOverlappingWindows(sponsorKey, ch, startMs, endMs, null);
            if (!overlaps.isEmpty()) throw unprocessable("WINDOW_OVERLAP", ...);
        }
        long id = repo.insertWindow(windowKey, 1, sponsorKey, businessDay, startMs, endMs, nowMs());
        for (ch : channels) repo.insertWindowChannel(id, ch);
        return toWindowResponse(...);
    });
}
```

Wait — validation order: "涉及多对象时先验证完整后态，再在一个事务内提交". 422 checks: empty channels → WINDOW_CHANNELS_EMPTY; time invalid → WINDOW_TIME_INVALID (end<=start, with actual/required in message); crosses day → 422 WINDOW_CROSSES_DAY. These should come before existence checks? Order: 422 param-shape checks first (empty channels, time), then channel existence 404, then duplicate key 409, then overlap 422. Reasonable.

Note: empty channels — request.channels() could be empty list → 422. Null handled by @NotNull → 400. Blank sponsorKey → @NotBlank 400.

Time invalid message with actual/required: "排他窗结束必须大于开始（实际时长 " + durationMs + " 毫秒，要求为正数）". Good — "数量和时长结果返回实际值、要求值或差额".

Window within business day: startMs >= dayStart && endMs <= dayEnd else 422 WINDOW_CROSSES_DAY.

Revise:
```java
@Transactional
public SponsorWindowResponse reviseSponsorWindow(String windowKey, ReviseSponsorWindowRequest request) {
    hash = sha256(OP_REVISE_WINDOW + "|" + windowKey + "|" + ...);
    idempotent(...) {
        validateWindowParams(...);
        SponsorWindowRow current = repo.findLatestWindowForUpdate(windowKey).orElseThrow(404);
        if (!current.status equals ACTIVE) throw conflict("WINDOW_NOT_ACTIVE", "排他窗已删除，不能修订");
        channels exist 404; lock channels (union of old and new channels? lock new channels sorted; old window row locked already);
        overlap check excluding own key;
        repo.supersedeWindow(current.id());
        long id = repo.insertWindow(windowKey, current.version()+1, ...);
        insert channels;
        return response;
    }
}
```

Delete:
```java
idempotent(OP_DELETE_WINDOW, hash=sha256(OP+windowKey)) {
    SponsorWindowRow current = repo.findLatestWindowForUpdate(windowKey).orElseThrow(404);
    if (!ACTIVE) throw conflict("WINDOW_NOT_ACTIVE", "排他窗已删除: " + windowKey);
    repo.deleteWindow(current.id());
    return toWindowResponse with DELETED status;
}
```

Get window:
```java
@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public SponsorWindowResponse getSponsorWindow(String windowKey) // latest version any status, 404
```

List windows:
```java
@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public List<SponsorWindowResponse> listSponsorWindows(String channelId, LocalDate businessDay) // channel must exist? 404 if not. Return ACTIVE windows for channel+day.
```

Override window check in doCreateOverride: after grant checks, before/after overlap check:
```java
String sponsorKey = repo.findAsset(request.assetId()).map(AssetRow::sponsorKey).orElse(null);
if (sponsorKey != null) {
    List<SponsorWindowRow> windows = repo.findActiveWindowsAt(channelId, startMs, endMs);
    for (w : windows) if (!w.sponsorKey().equals(sponsorKey)) → throw sponsorConflict 409 with details
}
```
Note asset existence already checked earlier in doCreateOverride (findAsset empty → 404). I'll fetch the asset row once and reuse.

Where exactly: after fallback-asset check we have asset. Currently code: `if (repo.findAsset(request.assetId()).isEmpty()) throw notFound`. I'll change to `AssetRow asset = repo.findAsset(...).orElseThrow(...)`.

Also override idempotency replay of EmergencyOverrideResponse — unchanged.

Publish changes: current publish() method — I'll rewrite it to use validate+commit helpers. Also hash for publish idempotency unchanged.

Also `insertPublicationSegment` signature changed → update publish commit.

PublicationRow constructor changed → check other usages: playoutDecision uses publication.get().id() only. OK.

AssetRow changed → createAsset, createChannel (uses findAsset only for existence), validateSegments (existence), doCreateOverride. Update createAsset response.

Now imports for service: SponsorWindowRow, WindowHitRow, new DTOs, List already there, LinkedHashSet/TreeSet maybe, Map/HashMap/LinkedHashMap for dedup.

Let me now write the service edits in chunks. Chunk 1: imports + createAsset + ApiException change (separate file). Chunk 2: publish refactor + batch + revoke + get publication. Chunk 3: windows section + override check.

First ApiException: add details field.

